{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>Let her not, I pray, be like the dead who, when he came forth from his mother's womb, had half his flesh eaten away.</b> Consider the stillborn who is dead in this manner: that upon emerging from his mother's womb half his flesh is eaten and corrupted. Even though he appears to add perfection at birth beyond what he had in his mother's womb — for he is going forth from there to the place of complete life — he in truth adds diminution, since half his flesh is eaten away at that very birth. So too you: you who go forth from the wilderness and enter the chosen land, and thereby improve the place of your dwelling — let it not be, I pray, as with that dead one, that you leave half your flesh in the wilderness."], :book :numbers, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:39:31.890057253Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}